  "doc": "Normal hydrogen is a 3:1 blend of ortho- and parahydrogen (see mp.H2_1 and mp.H2_2).  The normal hydrogen model is adapted from [1].  Calculated values agree with tabulated values in the original work to within a rounding error; believed to be caused by the precise choice of molecular mass (not reported).\n\n[1] J. Leachman, R. Jacobsen, S. Penoncello, E. Lemmon, Fundamental equations of state for parahydrogen, normal hydrogen, and orthohydrogen, Journal of Physical and Chemical Reference Data, v38, pp721, 2009.  doi:10.1063/1.3160306",
